From: limina <gustavo@noronha.eti.br>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/virtio: attach a fence to blob-scanout RESOURCE_FLUSH (limina #8 half 2)

virtio-gpu delivers flip-completion events from drm_atomic_helper_fake_vblank
(no vblank support), i.e. at commit-tail time, decoupled from anything the
host does. The only host-pacing lever in the driver is the dumb-buffer path:
prepare_fb attaches a per-FB fence, RESOURCE_FLUSH carries it, and
virtio_gpu_resource_flush dma_fence_wait()s (50 ms cap) before commit-tail
completes - so the host's fence response gates the (fake) flip event.

Host3d blob scanouts (venus) get neither: prepare_fb bails early for primary
planes unless bo->guest_blob, so their flushes are unfenced and the guest
repaints buffers on its own clock while the host compositor may still be
sampling them (limina rounds 21/22: stale-frame flicker on the zero-copy
display path; host-side present timing alone proven insufficient).

Give host3d blob primary-plane FBs the same fence the dumb path has. On a
host that completes fences at command execution (QEMU, crosvm, stock
libkrun) the wait returns immediately - behavior unchanged. A host that
understands the fence as a present gate (limina's LIMINA_FENCE_PRESENT path) can
delay its response until the frame is actually on glass, giving the guest
honest flip pacing and race-free buffer reuse.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_plane.c
@@ -254,10 +254,11 @@
 
 	vgfb = to_virtio_gpu_framebuffer(new_state->fb);
 	bo = gem_to_virtio_gpu_obj(vgfb->base.obj[0]);
-	if (!bo || (plane->type == DRM_PLANE_TYPE_PRIMARY && !bo->guest_blob))
+	if (!bo || (plane->type == DRM_PLANE_TYPE_PRIMARY && !bo->guest_blob &&
+		    !bo->host3d_blob))
 		return 0;
 
-	if (bo->dumb && (plane->state->fb != new_state->fb)) {
+	if ((bo->dumb || bo->host3d_blob) && (plane->state->fb != new_state->fb)) {
 		vgfb->fence = virtio_gpu_fence_alloc(vgdev, vgdev->fence_drv.context,
 						     0);
 		if (!vgfb->fence)
